    "text": "Andrei Stoica\nProduct minded full - stack software engineer with 4 years of experience in Product and VC\nandrei.bio andreicstoica@icloud.com /andrei-c-stoica (971) 312-7743\n\nProfessional Experience\nIndependent Contractor Full Stack & AI Engineering Sep ‘25\n- Stance Health: Rebuilt patient landing and results pages focusing on mobile (React/Chakra /Fast API/Next .js), reducing API over-fetching.\nAchieved 10x faster load times on form results page, improving drop off 8% during onboarding . Landing pages are now mobile friendly.\n- Holdfast: Architected research collaboration tool for NOA A-backed aquaculture grants (Postgres, tRPC). Enabled 20+ researchers to co-develop\nproposals, see shared resources, and streamline multi-institution submissions. Used MapLibre to create a collaborative resource map.\n\nFractal Tech Software Engineering Program Jun ‘25 - Aug ‘25\nSpent 60hrs /wk learning new web technologies, modern patterns, and how to build intuitive products with AI features.\nSelected Projects:\nRefract: Journal that pushes you deeper . E ngine - driven LLM generated ‘ nudges ’ , and clustered embeddings to analy z e themes af ter writing .\nCour tly: AI-gen practice sessions structured around given focus in an i O S and web app. C ollectible badges for popular NYC cour ts .\nBlob Must Grow: Clicker game in the browse r, inspired by C ookie C licker and Universal P aperclip. C omplex state management and engine .\nAlgos, Visualized: S tep by step visualizations of algorithms . Used W eb C anvas for visuals for D i j kstra ’ s and C onvex H ull , motion for Q uick Sor t .\n\nNBCUniversal Product Manager - Journalism Tools\nAug ‘24 - Jun ‘25\nDirected vendor analysis for newsroom people, places, and things scheduling system. Recommending $2M decision for a new global workflow.\nLed discover y and scoping of AI - aided fact - checking for j ournalists and producers, custom Google C loud LLM system with NBC U DB of facts.\n\nWarner Bros. Discovery Assoc. Product Manager - DTC/Digital July ‘2 3 - Aug ‘24\nOrchestrated accessibility, compliance, tech-debt, and multi-platform feature roadmaps across 20+ TVE (TNT , TLC , Discovery, HGTV) brands.\nDelivered 18% increase in app store rating ratio by solving 10+ consumer facing bugs and releasing 2 new features on mobile, TV, and web.\nImproved streaming per formance 6 2% by coordinating 3 engineering teams through a player and platform upgrade, rebasing 3 into 1 platform.\n\nBlocPower a16z Summer Intern Program Placement May ‘21 - Sep ‘21\nIncreased survey click - thru rate from 8% to 33% by implementing an end - page CTA and improved form UI, using Hotjar to analyze funnel .\nRe-designed Webflow website (site hierarchy, brand guidelines, CTAs, images) in preparation for national field enablement and ad campaign.\n\nAutodesk Growth Product Management Intern Jun ‘19 - Aug ‘19\nLaunched “Autodesk Day” events globally, where 400 users tested beta builds. Increased brand recognition and education partnerships.\nImproved task completion rates by 25% by orchestrating overhaul of the navigation bar and settings UI with feedback from beta testing .\n\nEducation\nNew York University Bachelor of Arts 2019-2023\nIndividualized Major: “Human-Computer Interaction and Ethical Innovati on Systems”\nRelevant Courses: AI and ML Topics, Discrete Math, Computer Systems Organization, Human-Centered Product Design, Statistics For Business\n\nHonors & Distinctions\nLexus Eco Challenge Finalist, $10,000 Prize: Pitched a green powered, off-the-grid shower, washer, and dryer system for the Portland\nhomeless. Funded by Lexus to finish building ‘ WashPod,’ which is still operational today.\nGoogle Cloud Covid-19 Hackathon Fund Finalist: Selected as the only Dubhacks 2020 finalist out of 400+ teams for creating a Covid-19 tool .\n\nSkills: React, Typescript, Next JS, Astro, React Native, Expo, Node.js, ExpressJS, Elysia, Better-Auth, JWT, PostgreSQL, Drizzle, Supabase, Web\nSockets, Biome, 